# React Development Patterns

## Component Structure
- Use functional components with hooks
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks when needed
- Use proper prop destructuring with TypeScript interfaces

## State Management
- Use useState for local component state
- Use useEffect for side effects and lifecycle management
- Implement proper cleanup in useEffect (return cleanup functions)
- Use useCallback and useMemo for performance optimization when needed

## Event Handling
- Define event handlers as arrow functions or useCallback
- Use proper TypeScript event types (React.ChangeEvent, React.MouseEvent, etc.)
- Implement proper event propagation control (stopPropagation, preventDefault)

## Component Communication
- Use props for parent-to-child communication
- Use callback props for child-to-parent communication
- Implement proper prop validation with TypeScript
- Use context for deeply nested component communication when needed

## Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement proper key props for list items
- Use lazy loading for large components when appropriate
- Avoid creating objects/functions in render methods

## Persian/Farsi Support
- All text content should be in Persian (Farsi)
- Use RTL (right-to-left) layout with `direction: rtl`
- Use Vazirmatn font family for Persian text
- Ensure proper text alignment and spacing for RTL content